{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4J6SViqF5oday3ku9F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient oak, iron-bound, weathered by centuries of hands pressing against its grain.*\n\n*A single keyhole glows faintly at its center, shaped like no key you've ever carried.*\n\n**You said \"key.\"**\n\n*But which key? A key is not a key until it fits. A word alone does not turn tumblers.*\n\n*The keyhole waits. The iron stays cold. The hinges do not sing.*\n\n**The lock remains.**\n\n*Try again. What opens me is not the name of the thing — it is the thing itself.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":134,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}